Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:46 +0100
Subject: NIFI-16547 Add connect timeout to cluster protocol sockets (#11924)

- Create an unconnected socket and connect with a timeout. The hostname is still resolved on every attempt and kept for TLS hostname verification.
- Add connectTimeout to SocketConfiguration, set from nifi.cluster.node.connection.timeout for the cluster protocol.
- Treat a connect timeout like a ConnectException when notifying the subject node of a status change, so it is not retried 5 times on the heartbeat monitor thread.

Signed-off-by: David Handermann <exceptionfactory@apache.org>
